counterfactuals.output:
A diagnostic method for a flow measurement system including a differential-pressure generator, the method comprising:

monitoring a pressure at a location downstream of the differential-pressure generator during a stabilization period in which a measured flow rate approaches a steady-state condition;

determining, based on the monitored pressure during the stabilization period, a controlled pressure value;

comparing the controlled pressure value with a predetermined normal pressure value;

determining a difference between the controlled pressure value and the predetermined normal pressure value; and

diagnosing a fault in the flow measurement system in response to the difference exceeding a predetermined threshold.
